From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:55:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 37/44] Camera: the item's change and the walking bob as in
 Minecraft

A new wielded item came in with Luanti's animation: the old one dropped
40 units in 0.125 s and the new one rose in another 0.125. Minecraft moves
the hand's height a tick at a time (FirstPersonHandsAndItems.tick): towards
0 while the item in hand isn't the one held, at most 0.4 a tick, the item
swapped once the height is under 0.1, then back towards the cube of the
attack's reload, drawn between the last two ticks. The same height already
lowered the item after a punch here; it now also does the change, at 20
ticks a second: 1, 0.6, 0.2, then 0 and the swap, then 0.4, 0.8 and 1, so
0.3 s in all. When a node is placed (Minecraft's itemUsed after a use that
changed the stack) the height drops to 0 at once and comes back up within
the swing.

Walking bobbed the view by Luanti's own amount (0.03 node to the side,
0.028 down, a slight roll) and the hand by 3 units. Minecraft bobs the
view and the hands together (GameRenderer.bobView): by its bob, which
eases 0.4 a tick towards the horizontal speed in blocks a tick, at most
0.1, on the ground (0 in the air, swimming, riding or dead), at the pace of
the distance walked times 0.6 (LocalPlayer.move): 0.5 bob to the side,
down by |cos| bob, turned by 3 bob degrees about the view and 5 |cos| bob
about its side axis. The view's camera moves by the inverse, so the world
bobs as in Minecraft; the hands, the arms holding a map, the map and the
off-hand item all bob with it. view_bobbing_amount still scales it (1.0,
the default, is Minecraft's; 0 turns it off). Footsteps sound at the same
pace (Entity.moveDist: every 1/0.6 node walked, the climb counted on a
ladder), as Luanti's animation did; a teleport doesn't count as a walk.

Checked in the native build at 640x480 with a log of every frame: a
sword swapped in takes 0.3 s and is swapped at the bottom; walking (W held
by xdotool, 4 m/s) the bob eases up to 0.1 and the distance walked grows by
2.4 a second, a step every 0.42 s, the hand and the view shifting by up to
0.05 block to the side and 0.1 down; a dirt block placed drops the hand and
brings it back in 0.15 s. Standing still, a sword, a dirt block, a torch,
the arm and the map draw as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

